# Template for .env â€” committed, placeholders only, never real keys.
#
#   cp .env.example .env        (PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)
#
# .env is gitignored. Put real keys there and nowhere else: not in source, not
# in a notebook cell, not in a commit message, not in a screenshot of a
# terminal. A key pasted into a public repo is compromised the moment it is
# pushed, and GitHub's history keeps it even after a later deletion.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING IN THIS PROJECT READS THESE YET.
#
# The assistant does not call an LLM. Each answer is stored in the corpus
# beside the URL it came from, so a citation cannot drift from the text above
# it (ARCHITECTURE.md section 4.1). Retrieval decides *which* stored fact to
# show; it never writes one. Adding a generation step is a real architectural
# change, not a config switch â€” see the note at the bottom.
#
# The embedding model runs locally and needs no key at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Provider ---------------------------------------------------------------
LLM_PROVIDER=gemini

# --- Gemini (the configured provider) ---------------------------------------
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# --- Generation settings ----------------------------------------------------
# Temperature 0 is the right default here. This assistant quotes published
# figures; there is nothing for sampling to improve and plenty for it to
# corrupt.
TEMPERATURE=0.0
MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=1024

# --- Optional: other providers, if you switch -------------------------------
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Local, no key required -------------------------------------------------
# The embedding model is downloaded once and cached; it never calls an API.
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2

# --- Backend selection (not a secret; here for convenience) -----------------
# tfidf (default, zero-install) | vector (MiniLM + ChromaDB)
# RETRIEVER_BACKEND=tfidf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you do wire an LLM in later, the thing to protect is the citation
# contract (PRD FR-11: exactly one source link on every answer, and it must
# support what the answer says). A generated answer can drift from the chunk
# it was built from while still carrying that chunk's link, which is worse
# than no answer â€” it is a wrong figure wearing an official document's
# authority. Whatever the generation step is, it needs a check that the cited
# URL came from the retrieved chunks, and that the claim is actually in them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
